---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteNav from '../components/SiteNav.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import PageScripts from '../components/PageScripts.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site.js';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/seo.js';

const navLinks = [
  { label: 'Repairs', href: '/repairs/' },
  { label: 'Shop', href: '/shop/' },
  { label: 'NBN Plans', href: '/nbn/' },
  { label: 'Blog', href: '/blog/' },
];

const schema = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy/' },
]);
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Express Repairs"
  description="How Express Repairs collects, uses and protects your personal information — enquiry forms, order requests, cookies and analytics."
  path="/privacy/"
  schema={schema}
  htmlAttrs={{ 'data-palette': 'electric-blue', 'data-fontpair': 'jakarta', 'data-dark': 'false' }}
>
  <SiteNav links={navLinks} ctaHref="/#contact" />

  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container-wide terms-wrap">
        <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <span class="crumb-sep">/</span>
          <span class="crumb-current">Privacy Policy</span>
        </nav>

        <h1 class="section-title" style="margin-top: 20px;">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="terms-updated">Effective 5 August 2026</p>

        <p>
          This policy explains how Mertel Pty&nbsp;Ltd (ABN 88&nbsp;644&nbsp;567&nbsp;019), trading as
          {SITE.name} ("we", "us"), of {SITE.addressShort}, handles personal information collected through
          this website and in store. We handle personal information in line with the Australian Privacy
          Principles in the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth). We've kept this in plain English on purpose.
        </p>

        <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Enquiry and booking forms</strong> — your name, phone number, email (optional), your device model, the repair or service you're asking about, and anything you type in the details box.</li>
          <li><strong>Shop order requests</strong> — the items you'd like to order, your name, phone, email (optional), and a delivery address if you choose delivery instead of pickup.</li>
          <li><strong>NBN sign-ups</strong> — covered separately in our <a href="/nbn/terms/">NBN Service Terms</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Website usage data</strong> — see cookies and analytics below.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We only ask for what we need to respond to you. You can always call or visit the store instead of
          using a form.
        </p>

        <h2>2. How we use it</h2>
        <p>
          Form submissions are emailed directly to our shop inbox so we can call or email you back about
          your enquiry or order. That's what the information is for — responding to you, confirming an
          order, and arranging your repair, pickup or delivery. We do not sell personal information, and we
          do not add you to marketing lists you didn't ask for.
        </p>
        <p>
          Separately from the email, we record an anonymised tally of enquiries (the enquiry type, device
          model and the ad campaign it came from — <strong>never</strong> your name, phone, email, address
          or message) so we can see which pages and ads are working.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Text messages.</strong> After a repair or an order we may send you one text message
          asking whether you'd leave us a Google review. It comes from the sender name "Xpress" and
          always carries an opt-out — call or text {SITE.phone} and we won't text you again. We don't
          send marketing texts. As with enquiries, we keep only an anonymised count that a message was
          sent — never your number or the message.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Who we share it with</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this website and processes form submissions at its edge network.</li>
          <li><strong>Resend</strong>, a transactional email provider, delivers your form submission to our inbox.</li>
          <li><strong>ClickSend</strong>, an SMS provider, delivers the review-request text message described above — it receives your mobile number and the message text.</li>
          <li><strong>Google</strong> — if you give us an email address with an online order, the Google Customer Reviews box on our order confirmation page passes that email address and your order number to Google, so Google can ask you to rate your experience. The box asks your permission first, and saying no means Google doesn't contact you.</li>
          <li>Service providers involved in fulfilling an order (for example, the postal carrier receives your name and delivery address to deliver a parcel).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These providers receive only what's needed to do their job. We don't otherwise disclose personal
          information unless the law requires it. Some providers (such as our website host and email
          provider) process data on servers located overseas, including in the United States.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Cookies, analytics and advertising</h2>
        <p>This site uses the following third-party measurement tools, which set cookies or similar identifiers:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> — anonymous statistics about how the site is used (pages visited, device type, general location).</li>
          <li><strong>Google Ads conversion tracking</strong> — records when a visit from a Google ad leads to a call or an enquiry, so we can measure our advertising.</li>
          <li><strong>Meta (Facebook) Pixel</strong> — records page views and enquiries from visitors who arrived via our Facebook or Instagram ads, for the same purpose.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Customer Reviews</strong> — on our order confirmation page only, a Google script draws the opt-in box described in section 3. It doesn't run anywhere else on the site.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We also keep a short-lived note in your browser's session storage of which ad or referring site
          brought you here, so an enquiry can be matched to the campaign that produced it. It's cleared when
          you close the browser tab and contains no personal details.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can block or clear cookies in your browser settings, use your browser's tracking protection,
          or opt out via <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google's Analytics opt-out</a>
          and your <a href="https://www.facebook.com/adpreferences/ad_settings" rel="noopener">Meta ad preferences</a>.
          The site works fine without them.
        </p>

        <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Enquiry emails are kept in our business inbox for as long as we need them to serve you and meet
          our record-keeping obligations. The anonymised enquiry tally is automatically deleted after two
          years. Records of actual purchases are kept as required by Australian tax law.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Security</h2>
        <p>
          The website is served over HTTPS, form submissions travel encrypted, and no payment details are
          ever collected on this website — we take payment in store or when we call to confirm your order.
          No system is perfectly secure, but we limit what we collect so there's little to lose.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Access, correction and complaints</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us at any time what personal information we hold about you, and ask us to correct or
          delete it — call {SITE.phone}, or drop into the store at {SITE.addressShort}. If you're not happy
          with how we've handled a privacy concern, you can complain to the Office of the Australian
          Information Commissioner (OAIC) at
          <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a> or on 1300&nbsp;363&nbsp;992.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we change this policy, the current version will always live at this page with an updated
          effective date.
        </p>

        <p class="terms-note">
          Questions? Call <a href={SITE.phoneHref}>{SITE.phone}</a> or visit us at {SITE.addressShort}.
        </p>

        <a href="/" class="btn btn-ghost" style="margin-top: 24px;">← Back to home</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
  <PageScripts />
</Layout>

<style>
  .terms-wrap { max-width: 760px; }
  .terms-wrap h2 { font-size: 22px; margin: 36px 0 12px; }
  .terms-wrap p, .terms-wrap li { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .terms-wrap ul { padding-left: 22px; margin: 12px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
  .terms-wrap a { color: var(--brand-700); font-weight: 600; }
  .terms-updated { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-subtle); margin: 8px 0 28px; }
  .terms-note { margin-top: 36px; font-size: 14px; }
</style>
